摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Harness engineering beginner tutorial, from 0 to 1","id":"gh:1195243030","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"learn-harness-engineering","slug":"walkinglabs/learn-harness-engineering","topics":["agent","agentic","agentic-ai","ai","ai-agent","ai-agents","dsh","dsh-plugin","harness","harness-engineering","harness-framework","llm"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Harness engineering beginner tutorial, from 0 to 1"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"A project-based course on building the environment, state management, verification, and control mech"},{"id":"p2s2","text":"anisms that make AI coding agents work reliably."},{"id":"p3s1","text":"> 🌍 This course is available in **15 languages**: English, 简体中文, 繁體中文, 日本語, 한국어, Español, Français, "},{"id":"p3s2","text":"Русский, Deutsch, العربية, Tiếng Việt, Oʻzbekcha, Türkçe, Portuguese (BR), Українська. Choose your l"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"anguage from the badges above."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"## 🆕 What's New — August 2026"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"**Frontier Harness Design Breakdowns — new section (4 breakdowns)**"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"| What | Details |"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| **New section** | Frontier Harness Design Breakdowns — Apply the course's five-subsystem framework"},{"id":"p7s2","text":" (instructions, tools, environment, state, feedback) to reverse-engineer how four frontier products "},{"id":"p7s3","text":"build real harnesses. |\n| **Pi** | How Pi builds its harness — a minimal kernel, programmable expans"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ion, and context engineering behind \"ask Pi to build what you want.\" |\n| **Claude Code** | How Claud"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"e Code builds its harness — four-layer memory, five-level compaction, hooks, and sub-agent isolation"},{"id":"p7s6","text":". |\n| **Codex** | How Codex builds its harness — the repository as source of truth, AGENTS.md as a d"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"irectory page, and worktree isolation. |\n| **DeepSeek** | How DeepSeek builds its harness — \"everyth"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"ing is a plugin,\" capability seams, and an event pipeline. |\n| **All 15 languages** | Full translati"},{"id":"p7s9","text":"on coverage across all supported languages. |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"**Key idea:** The course gives you a framework; these breakdowns show you how the same principles ac"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"tually play out in production harnesses."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"**Graph Engineering Update — 1 new lecture, 1 new project**"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| What | Details |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| **Lecture 14** | From Single Loops to Graph Engineering — Why a single loop grows into a graph: th"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"e four stacked layers (prompt → context → loop → graph) and where harness sits in that stack, the fo"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ur parts of a graph (nodes, edges, shared state, routing), why in-loop checkpoints can't fix the thr"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"ee structural failures at scale (Goodhart, blindness upward, conflict), a framework-agnostic six-ste"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"p walkthrough for building your first graph, graph vs. workflow, anchors, which open-source \"graph e"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"ngineering\" projects existed before the name vs. after it, the orchestration tax, and when a graph i"},{"id":"p11s7","text":"s actually worth drawing. |\n| **Project 08** | Draw Your Workflow as a Graph — Three progressive exp"},{"id":"p11s8","text":"eriments: draw your maker-checker loop as an explicit graph, add a parallel fan-out/fan-in node, the"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"n add a conditional rollback edge and a human-approval node. |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## 🆕 What's New — July 2026"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"**Loop Engineering Update — 1 new lecture, 1 new project**"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| What | Details |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| **Lecture 13** | Why You Need to Stop Prompting Your Agent — From `/goal` to the six primitives of"},{"id":"p16s2","text":" loop engineering (automations, worktrees, skills, connectors, sub-agents, external state), the gene"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"rator/evaluator split, four silent costs, and a step-by-step guide to building your first loop. |\n| "},{"id":"p16s4","text":"**Project 07** | Build Your First Automated Loop — Three progressive experiments: goal loop, timer l"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"oop, and maker-checker loop. Compare manual vs. automated, measure intervention reduction, and learn"},{"id":"p16s6","text":" to step outside the loop. |\n| **Code templates** | `goal-template.md`, `loop-state-template.md`, `m"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"aker-prompt.md`, `checker-prompt.md` — drop-in templates for building loops immediately. |\n| **All 1"},{"id":"p16s8","text":"5 languages** | Full translation coverage across all supported languages. |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"**Key idea:** Harness engineering builds the vehicle. Loop engineering designs the road it drives on"},{"id":"p17s2","text":" — and you design the road from outside the car."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Learn Harness Engineering is a course dedicated to the engineering of AI coding agents. We have deep"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"ly studied and synthesized the most advanced Harness Engineering theories and practices in the indus"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"try. Our core references include:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"- OpenAI: Harness engineering: leveraging Codex in an agent-first world\n- Anthropic: Effective harne"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"sses for long-running agents\n- Anthropic: Harness design for long-running application development\n- "},{"id":"p19s3","text":"Awesome Harness Engineering"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"> **Quick start?** The `skills/harness-creator/` skill can help you scaffold a production-grade harn"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ess (AGENTS.md, feature lists, init.sh, verification workflows) for your own project in minutes."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## What Harness Engineering Actually Means"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Harness engineering is about building a complete working environment around the model so it produces"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" reliable results. It's not about writing better prompts. It's about designing the system the model "},{"id":"p22s3","text":"s. It's not about writing better prompts. It's about designing the system the model operates inside."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"A harness has five subsystems:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Text version"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Each subsystem has one job:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- **Instructions** — Tell the agent what to do, in what order, and what to read before starting. Not"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" one giant file; a progressive disclosure structure the agent navigates on demand.\n- **State** — Tra"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ck what's been done, what's in progress, and what's next. Persisted to disk so the next session pick"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"s up exactly where the last one left off.\n- **Verification** — Only a passing test suite counts as e"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"vidence. The agent cannot declare victory without runnable proof.\n- **Scope** — Constrain the agent "},{"id":"p27s6","text":"to one feature at a time. No overreach. No half-finishing three things. No rewriting the feature lis"},{"id":"p27s7","text":"t to hide unfinished work.\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"This is a course where you actually run coding agents."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"You need at least one of these tools:"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- Claude Code\n- Codex\n- Another IDE or CLI coding agent that supports file editing, command executio"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"n, and multi-step tasks"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"The course assumes you can:"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"- Open a local repository\n- Allow the agent to edit files\n- Allow the agent to run commands\n- Inspec"},{"id":"p33s2","text":"t output and re-run tasks"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"If you don't have such a tool, you can still read the course content, but you won't be able to compl"},{"id":"p34s2","text":"ete the projects as intended."},{"id":"p35s1","text":"## Prerequisites"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"Required:"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"- Familiarity with the terminal, git, and local development environments\n- Ability to read and write"},{"id":"p37s2","text":" code in at least one common application stack\n- Basic software debugging experience (reading logs, "},{"id":"p37s3","text":"tests, and runtime behavior)\n- Enough time to commit to implementation-focused coursework"},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Helpful but not required:"},{"id":"p39s1","text":"- Experience with Electron, desktop apps, or local-first tools\n- Background in testing, logging, or "},{"id":"p39s2","text":"software architecture\n- Prior exposure to Codex, Claude Code, or similar coding agents"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
